      "title": "SMB2: Warn about nonzero ErrorContextCount with zero ByteCount",
      "message": "SMB2: Warn about nonzero ErrorContextCount with zero ByteCount\n\n[MS-SMB2] says that dialects before 3.1.1 MUST set ErrorContextCount\nto zero, and that dialect 3.1.1 sets it to a nonzero value, the\nErrorData of length ByteCount MUST be an array of ErrorContexts (each\nat least 8 bytes) with ErrorContextCount entries. It is thus\ninconsistent to have a zero ByteCount but a nonzero ErrorContextCount.\n\nHowever, some servers (such as Illumos's SMB server until recently) have\nbeen known to set ErrorContextCount to a bogus (uninitialized?) nonzero\nvalue with a zero ByteCount, particularly in cases where the SMB2 Header\nStatus field is a warning or otherwise an unsuccessful status but not\none of the specific error statuses listed in 2.2.2.2 with a defined\nErrorData structure. For those cases, add an expert info Warning but\nignore the ErrorContextCount value, treating it as if it were zero.\n\nFix #19410\n",
